# The shared desktop

One XFCE session runs on display `:1` for `{{ devbox_user }}`. People watch and use
it through noVNC, so what you open there is visible to them.

## Running GUI programs

`box exec COMMAND ...` runs a command inside that session's environment: display,
Xauthority, D-Bus session and the tool PATH. Without arguments it opens a shell
with the same environment. Use it for anything that opens a window and for tools
that talk to the session, such as the keyring.

    box exec firefox https://example.com
    box exec xvfb-run -a COMMAND ...     # a private display nobody sees

## Seeing and steering it

    box desktop screenshot --output /srv/agent/artifacts/screen.png
    box desktop click --args '{"x":300,"y":250}'
    box desktop type --args '{"text":"Hello"}'
    box desktop key --args '{"key":"ctrl+l"}'

`box desktop --help` lists everything. `xdotool` and `wmctrl` are installed too.
`box mcp` is the same as a stdio MCP server; its configuration is
`/etc/devbox/mcp.json`. `devbox-desktop` is the old name of `box desktop` and
still works.

## Sharing it

- Only one task should operate the desktop at a time. Calls are serialized.
- `box desktop pause` stops automated input while a person takes over, and
  `resume` allows it again. Respect a pause you did not set.
- A program waiting on a dialog blocks whoever started it. After starting a GUI
  program, take a screenshot and deal with what it shows.
